---
export const title = 'Usage';
export const order = 100;
import DemoComponentCard from '../../../../components/DemoComponentCard.astro';
---

<p>
  <code>wc-chat-message</code> is one turn of a conversation. <code>from="user"</code> shows the
  person's text in a bubble; the default, <code>from="assistant"</code>, shows the answer as formatted
  Markdown with its actions: copy, Try again and a good or bad rating.
</p>

<DemoComponentCard lang={'html'}>
  <div style='display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 1rem; inline-size: 100%; max-inline-size: 30rem;'>
    <wc-chat-message from='user' value='Will I get a loaner before Friday?'></wc-chat-message>
    <wc-chat-message id='message-answer' value='Desk support in Pune has **2 loaner laptops** free[1](cite:asset_9). Incidents raised before noon are usually handled the same day.'></wc-chat-message>
  </div>
  <script is:inline>
    (function () {
      var answer = document.querySelector('#message-answer');
      answer.citations = [{ id: 'asset_9', headline: 'Loaner pool · Pune', supportingText: 'Asset management' }];
      answer.addEventListener('feedback', function (event) {
        myConsole.log('feedback: ' + (event.detail.value || 'none'));
      });
      answer.addEventListener('regenerate', function () {
        myConsole.log('regenerate');
      });
    })();
  </script>
</DemoComponentCard>

<h3>Streaming</h3>
<p>
  While an answer arrives, set <code>streaming</code> and keep replacing <code>value</code>. Before the
  first words a typing indicator shows <code>status</code>. Actions appear once streaming stops.
</p>

<DemoComponentCard lang={'html'}>
  <wc-chat-message id='message-stream' streaming status='Checking loaner stock in Asset management…' style='inline-size: 100%; max-inline-size: 30rem;'></wc-chat-message>
  <wc-button id='message-stream-play' variant='text' size='sm' style='margin-top: 0.75rem;'>Play again</wc-button>
  <script is:inline>
    (function () {
      var el = document.querySelector('#message-stream');
      var text = 'Desk support has 2 loaner laptops free. Raise the incident before noon and pick one up at desk 4.';
      var timer;
      function play() {
        clearInterval(timer);
        el.value = '';
        el.streaming = true;
        var shown = 0;
        setTimeout(function () {
          timer = setInterval(function () {
            shown = Math.min(text.length, shown + 4);
            el.value = text.slice(0, shown);
            if (shown >= text.length) {
              clearInterval(timer);
              el.streaming = false;
            }
          }, 45);
        }, 1200);
      }
      document.querySelector('#message-stream-play').addEventListener('click', play);
      play();
    })();
  </script>
</DemoComponentCard>

<h3>Other people, and who wrote when</h3>
<p>
  <code>from="participant"</code> is another person in the conversation, such as a caller or a
  teammate: a quiet bubble at the start of the line, with their name above it. The line above a
  message also shows <code>channel</code> ("via Teams") and the time of <code>datetime</code>, and
  the <code>meta</code> slot adds a tag, such as "Work note". It appears for a participant, or once
  any of those is set, so a one-to-one conversation with the assistant stays bare.
</p>

<DemoComponentCard lang={'html'}>
  <div style='display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 1rem; inline-size: 100%; max-inline-size: 30rem;'>
    <wc-chat-message from='participant' author='Priya Shah' channel='Teams' datetime='2026-11-08T09:41:00' value='VPN drops every ten minutes for the whole Pune office.'>
      <wc-avatar slot='avatar' name='Priya Shah' size='sm'></wc-avatar>
    </wc-chat-message>
    <wc-chat-message from='user' author='Alan Kay' datetime='2026-11-08T09:50:00' value='Checked the gateway logs: the certificate expired at 09:30.'>
      <wc-tag slot='meta' size='sm'>Work note</wc-tag>
    </wc-chat-message>
  </div>
</DemoComponentCard>

<h3>Quick replies</h3>
<p>
  <code>suggestions</code> shows the likely next moves as chips under a finished message. Picking one
  fires <code>suggestion-select</code>; send it as the person's message and clear the list.
</p>

<DemoComponentCard lang={'html'}>
  <wc-chat-message id='message-quick' hide-actions value='Pune is back: 140 of 140 clients reconnected.' style='inline-size: 100%; max-inline-size: 30rem;'></wc-chat-message>
  <script is:inline>
    (function () {
      var message = document.querySelector('#message-quick');
      message.suggestions = ['Tell Priya', 'Mark CHG-311 as failed', 'Why did it expire?'];
      message.addEventListener('suggestion-select', function (event) {
        myConsole.log('suggestion-select: ' + event.detail.value);
      });
    })();
  </script>
</DemoComponentCard>

<h3>Steps, drafts and errors</h3>
<p>
  Put <code>wc-assistant-steps</code> in the <code>steps</code> slot, above the text, and
  <code>wc-draft-card</code>s in the default slot, below it. With <code>error</code> the message says
  the answer failed and offers Try again.
</p>

<DemoComponentCard lang={'html'}>
  <wc-chat-message error style='inline-size: 100%; max-inline-size: 30rem;'></wc-chat-message>
</DemoComponentCard>
